# tools/m/mycelium_till_knot_witness.rish — the treasury verdict reads across a Knot (Till r3).
#
# Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) · Mycelium consensus · Till rung r3 — across a Knot.
# r1 resolved a whole Cord Dag into a Till; r2 let it travel. Yet a treasury a family runs for years does
# not carry its whole past unbroken — the Knot (cord_knot.rye) ties off a committed prefix into a sealed
# FoldState so a bounded Dag runs forever. This rung makes the Till's corpus a Knot plus its live suffix.
#
# The crux this witness proves: a draw that won its coins inside a sealed checkpoint stays a winning draw
# when new facts continue the log, and a suffix draw the checkpointed treasury can no longer pay comes up
# SHORT across the cut exactly as it would within one unbroken resolution — a lawful no-op. A treasury of
# 1000 pays two prefix draws (100 + 700), sealed to a Knot at supply 200; the suffix draw of 700 finds only
# 200 yet the sealed issued is 1000, so it once could have been paid — a spent-out loss. The verdict never
# drifts: verdicts_match proves the full Cord and the Knot-continued resolution name the identical draws,
# loss, coins, supply, and loser. Integrity holds across the cut: a corrupt Knot refuses KnotCorrupt before
# a fact is folded, a tampered suffix fact refuses IdentityRefused, a never-could-pay draw (5000 past the
# sealed issued 1000) refuses Overdraw whole. Composes till + cord_knot + cord + fold public API only; demo
# keeper seeds — no key held.
#
# Scope: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-064129_mycelium-till-double-spend-exploration.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mycelium_till_knot_witness.rish

say "mycelium-till-knot: Language EN — a draw won inside a sealed checkpoint stays won; a draw the checkpointed treasury cannot pay comes up short across the cut."
say "mycelium-till-knot: Style Radiant — the Knot ties off a length of Cord and begins the next; the coin verdict reads one hand whether the win lives in a full Cord or a sealed Knot."
say "mycelium-till-knot: Lens TAME — the verdict never drifts across the cut; a corrupt Knot, a tampered suffix fact, a never-could-pay draw each refuse whole; demo seeds only, no key held."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mycelium/bin/till_knot"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/till_knot.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "mycelium-till-knot: build failed"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "mycelium-till-knot: selftest exited non-zero"
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-till-knot: selftest did not speak GREEN"
assert selftest.out contains "comes up short" else "mycelium-till-knot: spent-out-across-cut claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "reads the same across the cut" else "mycelium-till-knot: verdict-never-drifts claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "each refuse whole" else "mycelium-till-knot: integrity-refusal claim missing"

# The Till whose verdict continues, and the Knot that seals the past, both stand at the door.
let till = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/till.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/till && mycelium/bin/till 2>&1"]
assert till.ok else "mycelium-till-knot: the Till whose verdict continues is not GREEN"
assert till.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-till-knot: the Till did not speak its GREEN"

let knot = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/cord_knot.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/cord_knot && mycelium/bin/cord_knot 2>&1"]
assert knot.ok else "mycelium-till-knot: the Knot that seals the past is not GREEN"
assert knot.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-till-knot: the Knot did not speak its GREEN"

say "mycelium-till-knot: GREEN — the treasury verdict reads across a sealed checkpoint, the winning draw and the spent-out loss the same whether in a full Cord or a Knot; corruption refuses whole; the Till and the Knot stand at the door."
